Parameter data used by the core packages is drawn from published sources with no redistribution
restrictions. Values are transcribed with citations recorded in docs/sources/bibliography.md:

  - de Leva, P. (1996). Adjustments to Zatsiorsky-Seluyanov's segment inertia parameters.
    Journal of Biomechanics 29(9), 1223-1230.
  - Gordon, C. C., et al. (2014). 2012 Anthropometric Survey of U.S. Army Personnel (ANSUR II).
    US Army Natick Soldier RD&E Center. US federal government work.
  - Wu, G., et al. (2002, 2005). ISB recommendations on joint coordinate system definitions.
    Journal of Biomechanics 35(4) and 38(5).
  - Rajagopal, A., et al. (2016). Full-body musculoskeletal model for muscle-driven simulation of
    human gait. IEEE TBME 63(10), 2068-2079. Model freely distributed via SimTK.

Third-party software dependencies:

  - Rapier (dimforge) - Apache-2.0
  - MuJoCo (Google DeepMind) - Apache-2.0
  - three.js - MIT

No copyleft or non-commercially-licensed material enters the core packages. See ADR-009.
